    "description": "A code point is a numerical value that represents a specific character in an encoding system, such as Unicode. Each character, symbol, or control command in a character set is assigned a unique code point, allowing it to be stored and transmitted in digital systems.\n\nIn Unicode, code points are written as U+ followed by a hexadecimal number. For example, the character ``A`` has the code point ``U+0041``.",
